(963552, 113452, 24407, '<td valign="top">maybe a different crop would work better, panoramic just below the reflections, good shot!</td>', 'maybe a different crop would work better, panoramic just below the reflections, good shot!', '2004-10-18 07:09:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(963555, 113518, 16004, '<td valign="top">There are certain details in this shot that makes it overall quite appealling.  the colour and lighting on the damp cobbles is particularly gratifying, and i love the shadow cast by the gate on the pavings.  Having the grey-haired person works, too.  Unfortunately though, it all seems a little messy as you look further back.  This could do with a being a little sharper, either by using a tripod (or any flat stable surface - personally Im always on the look out for rubbish bins and other street furniture) or possibly a higher aperture (it seems quite shallow because the cobbles do appear to be in focus).  this has a load of potential but let down by a few factors put of your control - for example, it''s a pity that the detail of the ironwork at the top of the arch has been lost...  did you try adjusting this to a sepia tone?  the lights and darks might lend itself to a successful adjustment.  overall good - 5.</td>', 'There are certain details in this shot that makes it overall quite appealling.  the colour and lighting on the damp cobbles is particularly gratifying, and i love the shadow cast by the gate on the pavings.  Having the grey-haired person works, too.  Unfortunately though, it all seems a little messy as you look further back.  This could do with a being a little sharper, either by using a tripod (or any flat stable surface - personally Im always on the look out for rubbish bins and other street furniture) or possibly a higher aperture (it seems quite shallow because the cobbles do appear to be in focus).  this has a load of potential but let down by a few factors put of your control - for example, it''s a pity that the detail of the ironwork at the top of the arch has been lost...  did you try adjusting this to a sepia tone?  the lights and darks might lend itself to a successful adjustment.  overall good - 5.', '2004-10-18 07:13:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(963559, 113634, 16004, '<td valign="top">This is very dark (in a good way, dark in spirit not in lighting) and atmospheric.  So much about this i love - the non-perfect fence, the muted colours,  the way the tree is lit, the walls of the building.  The angle of the shot (especially regarding the biulding) is fantastic.  the silhouette of your title is a little superfluous really, i think the whole shot says so much already.  I think i might have been tempted to crop out the lamp at the top - it''s a bit too bright and quite a distraction.  I think i would have cropped the top of the shot 1 or 2mm below the bottom of the lamp.  also, though the border is a little fussy, it seems to work well.  9.</td>', 'This is very dark (in a good way, dark in spirit not in lighting) and atmospheric.  So much about this i love - the non-perfect fence, the muted colours,  the way the tree is lit, the walls of the building.  The angle of the shot (especially regarding the biulding) is fantastic.  the silhouette of your title is a little superfluous really, i think the whole shot says so much already.  I think i might have been tempted to crop out the lamp at the top - it''s a bit too bright and quite a distraction.  I think i would have cropped the top of the shot 1 or 2mm below the bottom of the lamp.  also, though the border is a little fussy, it seems to work well.  9.', '2004-10-18 07:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(963565, 113663, 10390, '<td valign="top">If you would crop this photo so the waterfall (?) to the right and the light to the left in the frame wouldn''t be seen, I think this photo would improve.  Even just using just a narrow framing on this I think it could make an outstanding photo.  A great motive that you had there, I wish I could have something like this to play with. Well seen motive, nice try.</td>', 'If you would crop this photo so the waterfall (?) to the right and the light to the left in the frame wouldn''t be seen, I think this photo would improve.  Even just using just a narrow framing on this I think it could make an outstanding photo.  A great motive that you had there, I wish I could have something like this to play with. Well seen motive, nice try.', '2004-10-18 07:35:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(963568, 113073, 10390, '<td valign="top">I think the light distracts too much, also there is a distracting noise in this photo. Otherwise, this is a well seen motive, beautiful colors.</td>', 'I think the light distracts too much, also there is a distracting noise in this photo. Otherwise, this is a well seen motive, beautiful colors.', '2004-10-18 07:39:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(963570, 113167, 16004, '<td valign="top">Very very nice.  gorgaous skyline here.  Personally, i would have liked the sculpture / reflective element to fill more of the screen, but overall i like the look of the shot.  quite unique, i love the distortion of the skyline and the clarity / sharpness is great.  8.</td>', 'Very very nice.  gorgaous skyline here.  Personally, i would have liked the sculpture / reflective element to fill more of the screen, but overall i like the look of the shot.  quite unique, i love the distortion of the skyline and the clarity / sharpness is great.  8.', '2004-10-18 07:42:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(963571, 113085, 10390, '<td valign="top">Nice photo, although I think it could be better if you would have cropped out some of the river in the foreground, maybe half of it.</td>', 'Nice photo, although I think it could be better if you would have cropped out some of the river in the foreground, maybe half of it.', '2004-10-18 07:43:24.000000', NULL, 1),
