(964090, 113024, 3569, '<td valign="top">Great shot....</td>', 'Great shot....', '2004-10-18 16:56:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(964091, 113641, 18197, '<td valign="top">Focus and DOF seem okay. Color is okay. Subject is weak. Comp is somewhat weak. Title, while possible appropriate to the subject, really doesn''t help place the photo in context or improve my understanding of what you''re trying to say. Sorry to seem negative. Just my opinion.</td>', 'Focus and DOF seem okay. Color is okay. Subject is weak. Comp is somewhat weak. Title, while possible appropriate to the subject, really doesn''t help place the photo in context or improve my understanding of what you''re trying to say. Sorry to seem negative. Just my opinion.', '2004-10-18 16:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(964092, 113687, 3569, '<td valign="top">Excellent in all ways</td>', 'Excellent in all ways', '2004-10-18 16:56:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(964094, 113504, 3102, '<td valign="top">I wouldn''t want to deal with the constant cold weather, but I''m definitely jealous of folks that get to see incredible things like this up north!  This is a really cool shot -- I love the exposure, and the way you incorporated the weeds in the foreground.  I suspect this will do very well this week.  It''s my only 10 so far.</td>', 'I wouldn''t want to deal with the constant cold weather, but I''m definitely jealous of folks that get to see incredible things like this up north!  This is a really cool shot -- I love the exposure, and the way you incorporated the weeds in the foreground.  I suspect this will do very well this week.  It''s my only 10 so far.', '2004-10-18 16:57:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(964095, 113167, 3102, '<td valign="top">I remember seeing this thing in the news just recently, and I was even thinking that it would certainly make an interesting DPC image.  It almost looks like some sort of funky Photoshop effect, doesn''t it?  Nice job with the exposure, etc.  Very cool shot!</td>', 'I remember seeing this thing in the news just recently, and I was even thinking that it would certainly make an interesting DPC image.  It almost looks like some sort of funky Photoshop effect, doesn''t it?  Nice job with the exposure, etc.  Very cool shot!', '2004-10-18 16:59:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(964103, 113504, 20754, '<td valign="top">a very lovely magical shot...great colors/composition...the wonderfully shaped silhoutted tree tops really add the extra spice to the shot for me..without those contrasting against the northernlights itwould have made for a bit of a blander photo...great job..one of my faves!</td>', 'a very lovely magical shot...great colors/composition...the wonderfully shaped silhoutted tree tops really add the extra spice to the shot for me..without those contrasting against the northernlights itwould have made for a bit of a blander photo...great job..one of my faves!', '2004-10-18 17:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(964104, 113362, 13136, '<td valign="top">There seems to be a haze over the upper half of the subject''s body.</td>', 'There seems to be a haze over the upper half of the subject''s body.', '2004-10-18 17:04:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(964105, 113315, 19445, '<td valign="top">Very nice - and very seasonally appropriate</td>', 'Very nice - and very seasonally appropriate', '2004-10-18 17:05:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(964106, 113349, 19445, '<td valign="top">no bowlers?</td>', 'no bowlers?', '2004-10-18 17:05:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(964109, 112544, 18197, '<td valign="top">I just recalibrated my monitor, as I do 2-3 times a day depending on the time of day and sun/clouds. So I don''t think that''s the problem. This is just to dark to make out enough detail to resonate with the photo. It could be your monitor needs recalibration.  I also copied your image into PS CS and used levels to adjust it to 0,1,114 across RGB and it works a lot better for me that way. Sorry to seem negative. It''s just my opinion.</td>', 'I just recalibrated my monitor, as I do 2-3 times a day depending on the time of day and sun/clouds. So I don''t think that''s the problem. This is just to dark to make out enough detail to resonate with the photo. It could be your monitor needs recalibration.  I also copied your image into PS CS and used levels to adjust it to 0,1,114 across RGB and it works a lot better for me that way. Sorry to seem negative. It''s just my opinion.', '2004-10-18 17:07:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(964122, 113348, 27524, '<td valign="top">Original idea of night shoot. Angle and colors are real wonderful.</td>', 'Original idea of night shoot. Angle and colors are real wonderful.', '2004-10-18 17:14:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(964123, 113429, 18197, '<td valign="top">I like the subject and composition of this image but IMO it''s just too bright. I just recalibrated my monitor so I don''t think that''s the problem. First I respect artistic integrity. You may have intended it to be ultra-bright. But in case that wasn''t your intention, I did play around with a copy of your photo a bit and a levels adjustment would made it more dramatic and toned it down a bit. I tried 50-100, 1.0, 255 across the RGB channels and got results more to my liking. Hope I didn''t offend you. It''s just my opinion after all.</td>', 'I like the subject and composition of this image but IMO it''s just too bright. I just recalibrated my monitor so I don''t think that''s the problem. First I respect artistic integrity. You may have intended it to be ultra-bright. But in case that wasn''t your intention, I did play around with a copy of your photo a bit and a levels adjustment would made it more dramatic and toned it down a bit. I tried 50-100, 1.0, 255 across the RGB channels and got results more to my liking. Hope I didn''t offend you. It''s just my opinion after all.', '2004-10-18 17:14:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(964124, 113563, 18197, '<td valign="top">Kinda reminds me of finger painting in grade school. Only I never got to finger paint with light. Thanks for the nostalgia trip.</td>', 'Kinda reminds me of finger painting in grade school. Only I never got to finger paint with light. Thanks for the nostalgia trip.', '2004-10-18 17:16:20.000000', NULL, 1),
