(972057, 113533, 4877, '<td valign="top">Hey!  This is a great shot!  <br/> <br/>Well exposed, and love the tracking motion!  Its difficult to get a good tracking shot during the day, let alone at night!<br/> <br/>Great job!  Good luck!</td>', 'Hey!  This is a great shot!   Well exposed, and love the tracking motion!  Its difficult to get a good tracking shot during the day, let alone at night! Great job!  Good luck!', '2004-10-24 21:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(972059, 113641, 21714, '<td valign="top">I can''t associte this picture with a night shot. Not saying that it wasn''t taken after the sun went down. But, the colours don''t really give the sense of night. And I do not find the subject or composition interesting. <br/>I think (if there was enough room for you to get the whole cross in the frame) a portrait or vertical shot would have worked better. Also, the sky if it was a bit darker would have made you feel more like you are looking at a night scene. <br/>Usually, the sky is something that we see almost every day and it doesn''t change much. To make something like the sky interesting with an object like the cross you have used, I think you would need to make it stand out - created some contrast for it to look interesting to the viewer.  All the best with future projects.</td>', 'I can''t associte this picture with a night shot. Not saying that it wasn''t taken after the sun went down. But, the colours don''t really give the sense of night. And I do not find the subject or composition interesting. I think (if there was enough room for you to get the whole cross in the frame) a portrait or vertical shot would have worked better. Also, the sky if it was a bit darker would have made you feel more like you are looking at a night scene. Usually, the sky is something that we see almost every day and it doesn''t change much. To make something like the sky interesting with an object like the cross you have used, I think you would need to make it stand out - created some contrast for it to look interesting to the viewer.  All the best with future projects.', '2004-10-24 21:27:19.000000', NULL, 1),
